[IMG]https://www.maketecheasier.com/assets/uploads/2019/01/twrp-featured.jpg[/IMG]

Team Win Recovery Project (TWRP) is an open-source software custom recovery image for Android-based devices. It provides a touchscreen-enabled interface that allows users to install third-party firmware and back up the current system, functions often unsupported by stock recovery images. It is, therefore, often installed when rooting Android devices, although it isn't dependent on a device being rooted to be installed.

Functional on both Y210-0010 and Y210-2010 models.

[SIZE="5"][B]Instructions[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST=1]
[*]Download the recovery image below.
[*]Download [URL="https://developer.android.com/tools/releases/platform-tools"]fastboot[/URL] on your computer.
[*]Reboot into bootloader mode with Volume Down + Power buttons.
[*]Flash the recovery image with fastboot: [CODE]fastboot flash recovery twrp-3.1.1-y210.img[/CODE]
[*]Reboot into recovery mode with Volume Up + Power buttons.
[*]SUCCESS! You have successfully installed TWRP and can use it for anything (as long as it isn't listed in the Current Issues section).
[/LIST]

[SIZE="5"][B]Current Issues[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]None! All features are working properly.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="5"][B]What's Working[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Boot to recovery
[*]Mount /system, /data and /cache
[*]Nandroid backup and restore
[*]Install zip packages
[*]Wipe cache and data
[*]ADB in recovery
[*]Offmode charging
[/LIST]

